## 14. Attestation and notices

On written request from LIL, not more than once a year unless it reasonably suspects material breach, an authorized representative of Yours will attest within thirty days to compliance. If reasonably necessary to resolve specific material concerns that the attestation does not resolve, LIL or the Foundation may inspect relevant compliance records, on reasonable notice and under confidentiality safeguards, using an independent reviewer where appropriate. The request must identify the concern and be proportionate; it grants no unrestricted system access, continuous telemetry or right to demand unrelated information. You need not disclose source code, privileged material, personal data, or confidential research or security information; reasonable redacted records or independent verification may be used instead. LIL and the Foundation keep non-public responses confidential except as needed for enforcement or required by law.

Notices and registrations to LIL go to org@sovfound.org until a replacement contact is published at the canonical program address. A contact change affects only later notices; it does not alter this License. Research and internal Evaluation Use require no account or registered notice address. Pilot contacts keep their designated address current. Individual notices are directed to Your last designated or otherwise reliably identified contact. Only a general preview-ending notice under Section 11.3 may be given by public posting alone; LIL also sends it to recorded pilot contacts. Individual ethics or safety notices must identify the conduct and effective date.

## 15. Versions

The Foundation's current license page at https://sovfound.org/licenses/ identifies the current working version and may change as feedback is evaluated. Each issued version has permanently archived, fixed text at its own address and an exact-text digest. A substantive correction or change creates a new version, never a silent replacement of existing terms. A Software release identifies its governing version. A later version governs that release only if You and LIL expressly elect it, or a separately executed grant expressly provides for that change. Changes to program guidance, working-group recommendations, registration forms or contact details do not change permissions already granted. A matching archived copy controls if the website is unavailable.

